+# Todo due date implementation plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional date-only due date (`dueDate`, `YYYY-MM-DD`); a todo that is not done and whose due date is strictly before today (UTC) is overdue — visible and filterable in the JSON API (`GET /todos?overdue=true`) and in the list page (date shown, "überfällig" marker, "nur überfällige" toggle).
+
+**Architecture:** `DateOnly? DueDate` is added to the `Todo` record; `IsOverdue()` is a computed method on the record (UTC "today", never JSON-serialized). `TodoStore` validates dates and applies PATCH semantics (absent = keep, explicit `null` = clear). The API adds the `overdue` query filter; the page filters client-side behind the toggle.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor Web App (interactive server render mode), minimal JSON API on the same `TodoStore`, xUnit + `WebApplicationFactory<Program>`, Playwright MCP for the end-to-end check.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-01-todo-due-date-design.md` (ticket #1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No new NuGet packages.
+- Validation errors are `System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations.ValidationException`, mapped in `Program.cs` to HTTP 400 `{"error": "..."}`; malformed JSON already maps to 400 via `BadHttpRequestException` (`ThrowOnBadRequest` is on).
+- TDD: failing test in `tests/` first, then the minimal implementation, then a green run, then a commit.
+- Every UI element tests rely on carries a `data-testid`.
+- "Today" is UTC: `DateOnly.FromDateTime(DateTime.UtcNow)`.
+- End-to-end: start the app as AGENTS.md describes, drive it with Playwright, screenshots outside the repo, stop the app.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- PATCH without `dueDate` must not clear an existing due date; explicit `"dueDate": null` must clear it (Task 2 tests).
+- A todo due today (UTC) is not overdue; only strictly past dates are (Task 1 tests).
+- A done todo with a past due date is not overdue (Task 1 tests).
+- Invalid dates (`"2026-02-30"`, `"30.02.2026"`, `"2026-11-05T10:00:00"`, a JSON number, `""`) are rejected with 400 on POST and PATCH (Tasks 1–2 tests).
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` and the "nur überfällige" toggle with nothing overdue yield an empty list (Tasks 2–3, E2E).
+
+---
+
